A||||32||kitcar||1/4 miles times/0-60 times...whats your best.......||||6||
Z||000000||kitcar||04-23-2001||07:04 PM||||What is your best 1/4 miles times, and 0-60 times.  Also what engine are you running on with the mods!!||||reg||6
Z||000001||Jay||04-23-2001||07:19 PM||||Last year before mods I ran a 13.8 @100mph<BR>This year we've estimated around 13.4 because of the exhaust work and shortened belt also intake.  I'm driving an 86 GT with a 4.6 Northstar STS engine. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  What are you running?<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>for photos goto: <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||kitcar||04-23-2001||07:26 PM||||Jay, good run!<P>I am not running anything yet at this time, i am about to install a 3.8 supercharged engine, and i was just wondering what are the times i would be running, so i was seeing what times you guys were hitting with the engines you have.<P>Could you est. what i would run?  My car weighs 2,300lbs with a 3.8Supercharged about to be installed!<P>Anyone else have times??<BR>What can be done to hit 12's<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||04-23-2001||10:28 PM||||2300 pnds?? What the heck did you cut off?<BR>If you're using the 4cyl weight you're way off, the V6 weighs more and the 3800 weighs<BR>even more than the 2.8.<BR>Normally 3800 SC's in Fieros are good for<BR>low to mid 13's depending on mods.<BR>Check out the latest Hot Rod mag. it has a<BR>3800 SC Formula in it.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jay||04-23-2001||10:45 PM||||It also depends on the driver.  There is a 3.8SC with Nos, port polished heads ect that can only manage low 14's (and that is with NOS!!) The most important piece of the 1/4 mile time is the driver.  If you can't shift good stay with an automatic!!!! By the way, what kind of kit are you doing?  I used to have a Ferrari Dino.||||reg||1
Z||000005||kitcar||04-24-2001||01:01 AM||||I think its light cause i have a diablo vt replica.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dave Gunsul||04-24-2001||09:04 PM||||If anything the kit you have should make it<BR>weigh more not less. <BR>If you have bigger wheels they too will make<BR>the car weigh more.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||04-25-2001||06:25 AM||||The Formula on Hot Rod is mine   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>BTW with me in it- weight is 3068 lbs<BR><P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">  <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||04-25-2001||07:23 AM||||The 2.5 weighs as much as the 2.8, well actually I think they are within 25 lbs.  I got that from Ed Parks when we were discussing shipping engines.<P>For the price of a Northstar conversion I would hope for more then 13s.  But thats just me.  I heard that there are computer issues that may limit the full potential of the motor in a Fiero, but Lingenfelter is helping Chris Moore with that (I suspect lower then 13s when they are done)<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||04-25-2001||08:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>The Formula on Hot Rod is mine    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>BTW with me in it- weight is 3068 lbs<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey, Phil, nice article.  It was great to read about your experiences on the tour, but I do wish they had gone into more detail about the car.  Basically all they said is you got a 3800SC Fiero, and it's fast.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  We KNEW that!  What's the best time you've run?  The article said, what, mid 13's?  And what kind of clutch are you using?  And real problems with longevity?  I'm looking at either a 3800SC or 3.4TDC swap for my Formula sometime in the future.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phil||04-25-2001||09:55 AM||||Actually they said mid 13 capable- my one and only run down the strip was frought with mistakes. I hit the rev limiter in both 1st and 2nd and the clutch wouldn't hold in 4th but managed a 14.3. Right now I have a McLeod clutch but I have a CF from V8 Archie that I'm going to put in someday. Takes a lot to hold back 277 crank HP  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Dave Gunsul||04-25-2001||08:34 PM||||Hey Phil, very nice car and article!!<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000012||Turbo1dr||04-26-2001||12:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kitcar:<BR><B>What is your best 1/4 miles times, and 0-60 times.  Also what engine are you running on with the mods!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Fiero's are conversation pieces. People don't drag race them often from what I've seen.<P><P>------------------<BR>86 SE Fiero converted to GT (Buick Turbo V6 transplant in progress)<P><B>78 Malibu</B> 3.8L Turbo Buick<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/turbowonder/Malibu/Homex.html" TARGET=_blank>TURBO WONDER</A><BR>Best 8th: 1.453, 6.53@107.39  3450lb<BR>TE-70 3 bolt, Ported Stock Iron Heads and Intake<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/turbowonder/Malibu/Modifications_files/Intercooler.jpg" TARGET=_blank>2.5 stock intercoolers</A><BR>Vernon Swindell, Jr.||||reg||1
Z||000013||northstar87||04-26-2001||10:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Turbo1dr:<BR><B> Fiero's are conversation pieces. People don't drag race them often from what I've seen.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Are you trying to start something?  It sounds like you have to rely on the turbo for you to be fast.  I will just stick with my normally asperated engine.  Why are you giving kitcar a hard time? He was just asking a question.  <BR>Chris <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Turbo1dr||04-26-2001||11:00 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by northstar87:<BR><B> Are you trying to start something?  It sounds like you have to rely on the turbo for you to be fast.  I will just stick with my normally asperated engine.  Why are you giving kitcar a hard time? He was just asking a question.  <BR>Chris </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not at all was I trying to give anyone a hard time.  From my surfing the web of most of the Fiero sites I see few owners who actually posts timeslips from going to the dragstrip. Don't see any time's in people's signatures either. For the most part I've gathered that most Fiero owners modify their cars to have a little more available power and to show them. That's why I said they are mostly conversation pieces and not a car that people modify to dragrace. If you look at this post you'll see that the responses was not what kitcar wanted. Only two people posted what he run and that was Jay and phil.  <P>BTW, I happen to like turbo's because they give you ultra high performance in a small engine capable of achiving upwards of 30mpg and still maintaining excellent drivability. There <I>IS</I> replacement for displacement!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>86 SE Fiero converted to GT (Buick Turbo V6 transplant in progress)<P><B>78 Malibu</B> 3.8L Turbo Buick<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/turbowonder/Malibu/Homex.html" TARGET=_blank>TURBO WONDER</A><BR>Best 8th: 1.453, 6.53@107.39  3450lb<BR>TE-70 3 bolt, Ported Stock Iron Heads and Intake<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/turbowonder/Malibu/Modifications_files/Intercooler.jpg" TARGET=_blank>2.5 stock intercoolers</A><BR>Vernon Swindell, Jr.<p>[This message has been edited by Turbo1dr (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||2
Z||000015||FieroSTETZ||04-27-2001||03:05 AM||||i don't know if it counts, but a while back someone posted a thing about renting a neon and nos'ing it - a friend and i wanted to try it, and just so happened i had a fiero with bad knocking (the car rocks to and fro) and i have the new motor ready to go in, so we set the thingy up, and my car ran 12.67 according to mr g tech, and i was able to drive the car home. the knocking is significantly worse now. i think i have video somewhere, recently moved and am still settling in <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460757&p=25516673&Sequence=0&res=high"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Jay||04-27-2001||04:05 PM||||STETZ, the G-tech is not an acurate enough instrument to determine 1/4 mile times.  We've used one at the strip and it was way off!!  Useful in some respects but I wouldn't trust the reading.<P>BTW there are lots of people who drag race their fiero's at the track.  Last year the GTA Fiero Club (Toronto) had about 10 fiero's show up for an event, from bone stock to turbo's they were all there representin'!  It's all about having a good time and not doing it on the street (at least not too hard on the street!).  It is fun to watch Fiero's smoke muscle cars and even, as was the case last year, a few lotus' that were there as part of their club, not to mention all of the Hondas and Acuras.  Not that there is anything wrong with Hondas, Acuras or Lotus'  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||drednot||04-27-2001||06:52 PM||||8.9 @ 169mph||||reg||1
Z||000018||Shaun41178||04-27-2001||07:08 PM||||14.1 @ 90mph<BR>85 Fiero GT'<BR>auto tranny<BR>stock 2.8<BR>custom cold ait<BR>ported exhaust manifolds<BR>nos 70 shot<BR>underdrive pulley<BR> <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> <P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Tryxalon||04-27-2001||10:30 PM||||Friend and I took his "G-tech" (digital dynometer?  Cool gadget!! Don't know how accurate.) and ran some tests today, his 83 RX-7 and <BR> My 85 Fiero SE 2.5L (Isuzu 5 speed) with 101,000 miles (tune up, all emissions working, factory specs).  <P>My Fiero results: Weight of car with both of us in it: 2875 lbs <P>0-60 and 1/4 mile times <BR>10.1    18.2 <BR>10.1    18.4<BR>9.8     17.5<BR>9.5     16.8 <BR>9.6     17.1 <P>(no HE didn't write down the 1/4 mile <B>speeds </B>- Well, he did, but I lost the scrap of paper they were written on!! <BR> duh??? kicking myself!!) <P>Not too bad for something that gets 25 MPG in town, eh?? <P>Oh, And guys, I found out that the engine's "notch" or point where torque is still as high as the horsepower has climbed to (after torque peak and before horsepower peak) on MY engine is about 3800 rpm ... which means most efficient shift point (balance of power) is there ... not at MAX HP. <P>My engine gets positively anemic above 4500 rpm!! (acts like its got a "truck" engine in it!! - but boy can it "pull!") <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Tryxalon (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Phil||04-27-2001||11:46 PM||||The weight sounds a trifle on the light side.||||reg||1
Z||000021||banditbalz||04-28-2001||12:55 AM||||15.2 @ 90 mph<BR>60 foot 1.92 sec<P>Cayuga Dragway Park, hot summer night 1999<P>4 speed Muncie (is there anything else?) and a stock engine. Car feels much quicker today with new motor mounts and clutch.<P>Yes, I am a GTA member.<P>Yes, we have a sub 10 second prostreet Fiero.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||14
Z||000022||88formula||04-28-2001||10:30 AM||||Your mph says you have more than 140 horsepower or a lighter fiero than stock. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||banditbalz||04-28-2001||07:45 PM||||higher mph = higher hp<P>I have owned this car for 9 years. As far as I know, the engine is stock. Although I started to wonder after my first summer of embarrasing 5.0L mustangs on the street and even more unbelievable, on the track.<BR>I think the secret is in my launches. Nothing beats the 4 speed Muncie for strength and long gearing. I shift early (usually 6000 in first, 5500 in second and hold it through third). I have stock 60 series 215 tires in back. I associate my higher than normal mph (should be around 86 mph) to my Holley scoop, K+N air filter, SplitFire spark plugs. The car feels FAST! It must have a cam or some other minor mod. I have pulled the front manifold and it is NOT ported.<P>I have one of my better timeslips posted on my Fiero page<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000024||88formula||04-28-2001||08:30 PM||||That is amazing. You would embarrass some 3.1 and some automatic 3.4 powered fiero's with that thing. Imagine what would happen if you ported the manifolds or added headers? <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Black88GT||04-28-2001||08:38 PM||||Embarassing 5.0s?  C'mon.  I'm sorry but there isn't a 5.0 around here that doesn't run 14s or lower.  15.2 is good enough for most ricers, but not Mustangs or F-bods.<P>Holley scoop adds 0 Hp.  K&N adds 1-2 Hp.  Spark plugs add 0 Hp.  <P>That trap speed is pretty high too for a 15.2 run.  I dunno something doesn't seem right.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||Jay||04-29-2001||05:16 PM||||I've seen Banditbalz car at the track.  I even sold him my rims.  His car is, for some unexplained reason a rocket!!No major mods that I could tell. <P>I have to disagree that a holley scoop K&N filter doesn't add any hp.  Mind you I have a Northstar, but the theory works on any car.  The cooler the air the denser it is.  More air=more hp.  The ability to consume that air and fuel mixture efficienty= more hp.  When I changed my intake, air filter and spark plugs  (platinum 4), I took 3/10 off of my time!  That is a fact, I changed them at the track to see if there was a difference.<P>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT  <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||BBBAD GT||04-29-2001||09:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by banditbalz:<BR><B>Although I started to wonder after my first summer of embarrasing 5.0L mustangs on the street and even more unbelievable, on the track.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No disrespect, but I'd be embarrased if I were driving the 5.0 and got smoked by a guy doing 15's.  The 5.0 around you aren't even in the 14's at the track?<BR><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000028||Slammed Fiero||04-29-2001||11:20 PM||||I have raced banditbalz too , he is an amazing drag racer , as for beating 5.0lt's I have a 5.0ltr in my driveway that gets beat by My fiero on a regular basis , Most of my friends late 80's hatchback cars run low 15's , there are a few serious 5.0's around , but I know who they are , and I show respect... Having driven a 5.0ltr on a regular basis (95 automatic) I can say my fiero feels quite a bit faster ..all depends ont he 5.0ltr and whats done to it..<P><BR>JM||||reg||1
Z||000029||Slammed Fiero||04-29-2001||11:25 PM||||Oh yeah , never run the 1/4 , But my best 0 to 60 on a GTEC has been 6.54 , Chris moore and Fierolisa can vouch for this , I have do mid / high 6's on average..<P><BR>JM <P>no 1/4 mile times as of yet , I suspect mid 15's<P>||||reg||1
Z||000030||I HATE V6 Fieros||04-29-2001||11:31 PM||||Iron Dukes rule!||||reg||8
Z||000031||grinthock||04-29-2001||11:44 PM||||Honestly?   I have to tell EVERYONE!  I live next door to BanditBalz and we hit the streets 2 or 3 days a week and we hit the track all the time, his usual times?  15.4's  I saw the 15.2, it WAS Real.   <P>ALSO, His car is STOCK, he has the airbox removed, stuff like that, but the car pulls NICE, it doesn't SOUND like it has a CAM, but MAYBE there was work done to it BEFORE he got it, but it looks BONE stock, even the FieroShop said they say something is up that they can't figure either, but we have searched and searched and it looks bone stock...<P>He is also an AMAZING drag driver, he shifts great and launched close to perfectly||||reg||1
Z||000032||grinthock||04-29-2001||11:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>It also depends on the driver.  There is a 3.8SC with Nos, port polished heads ect that can only manage low 14's (and that is with NOS!!) The most important piece of the 1/4 mile time is the driver.  If you can't shift good stay with an automatic!!!! By the way, what kind of kit are you doing?  I used to have a Ferrari Dino.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Jay you are SOOOO right, saw that guy run, he just needs to learn how to shift properly and stuff, I wish he owuld let one of us run it so we could show him what it can do!  Or let the guy who built it run it (but then again he never gets to run anything he builds!)<BR>||||reg||1
